one of the most lavish parties on new  year's eve 2012  started aboard a rented 747.  [Music]  the jet which was turned into a casino  flew to australia where attendees  including leonardo dicaprio and jamie  foxx rang in the new year aboard a yacht  then they quickly bundled back into the  747 flew to las vegas at the highest  speed possible  and were shuttled to a nightclub where  they were able to do the countdown again  they basically beat the clock despite  its celebrity filled guest list  this was no hollywood production the  host was a malaysian financier  joe lowe his fortune made the whole  thing happen  it also allegedly came from what appears  to be one of the biggest heists in  history  the 1mdb scandal the people who were  alleged to have  done this theft allegedly stole four and  a half billion dollars  that's a lot more than even some of the  worst dictators in history have stolen  lowe isn't alleged to have done this  alone goldman sachs and some of its  bankers are said to have played a key  role  the bank has just reached a  multi-billion dollar settlement with the  us government for its involvement  it touched wall street it touched  hollywood it went to vegas and there's  the most  powerful investment bank on the planet  right at the center of it  so let's take a look at the scheme that  allegedly helped fund that party and  many others  the players that allegedly benefited  from it and the fallout for them  and the bank as the plan began to  unravel  from the start 1mdb was a very strange  animal 1mdb which stands for one  malaysia development berhad was a  sovereign wealth fund created in 2009 by  prime minister najib razak  though it was low's idea and he ran the  fun behind the scenes when we think of  sovereign wealth funds we think of  a huge pot of money the savings account  of a country  but one mdb was part of a new class of  sovereign wealth funds that were kind of  in vogue  so the idea is you borrow money you're  paying the interest on it but the payoff  the benefit from the money you bought is  so much better that the economy is  better off for taking on this debt  1mdb touted big economic development  projects  including turning malaysia's capital  city kuala lumpur into the wall street  of asia  to borrow the money needed one mdb's  leadership turned to goldman sachs  and tim leisner the bank's chairman in  the region for goldman  there's two things at stake here there's  a lot of money  one mdb is willing to pay them uh huge  fees to raise money  quickly and quietly there's also this is  a new frontier for goldman  in asia they think there's going to be a  lot of investment a lot of economic  growth and they want to be the us  investment bank that's leading the way  in total goldman raised six and a half  billion dollars for one mdb  through three bond sales in 2012 and  2013. but what stood out were the fees  the bank collected on these deals  on the three deals goldman earned about  600 million dollars  that's ten times what banks typically  earn on bond issuances  it was a total red flag right it just  didn't make sense as we got deeper and  deeper and deeper into it  the more it didn't make sense  prosecutors now allege that some four  and a half billion dollars of the money  raised  was stolen siphoned off by low leisner  and others  but it would be another two years from  the time the bonds were issued before  the scheme  started to unravel when it really got  our attention though  was what i like to think of as the first  island on the archipelago  of scandals in 2015 the wall street  journal reported 1mdb  paid what appeared to be an inflated  price for power plants in malaysia  the fund purchased these assets from a  company that then used the overpayment  to make a donation to a charity chaired  by najib  that charity then used the money to fund  schools in districts where najib needed  votes  and then within weeks we got a tip  and we were able to get documents that  showed that  nearly 700 million dollars of money from  1mdb found its way into the prime  minister's bank account  and that was explosive to this day najib  denies wrongdoing  he previously claimed the 681 million  dollars was a donation from the king of  saudi arabia  but after the news broke the federal  bureau of investigation initiated a  probe into the affair  everybody knew that there was this one  mdb scandal kind of boiling there was  this scandal with the charities  but you couldn't connect them that's why  it was an archipelago with increased  scrutiny on 1mdb in its spending the  journal reported in 2015  that a 1.4 billion dollar payment 1mdb  had said it made to its partner in abu  dhabi  the international petroleum investment  company had gone missing  that payment was said to have been made  to an ipic subsidiary called  abar documents provided to the wall  street journal show that a payment was  made to abar investments limited  only problem there is no abbar  investments limited within the corporate  structure of abbar  and that was something that became a  pattern through all of our reporting we  found that there was these look-alike  companies frequently used and  that was a big revelation for us as its  scandals spread outside malaysia 1mdb  was struggling to repay more than 11  billion dollars in debt  because the money was stolen it wasn't  invested without investment returns the  fund couldn't pay back the bonds  eventually all of the islands in the  archipelago were connected when the  justice department  issued this huge complaint where they  explained all of the money flows that we  couldn't see behind the scenes  and low was allegedly at the center of  it all this guy  who was by all rights the mastermind  behind the fund  was buying luxury condos in new york and  london  he was throwing these you know crazy  parties in las vegas  and there was a pattern of behavior with  him and some other people that made it  clear  that um you know money came from  somewhere  and then there was this  low was also the financier behind a  little-known movie studio called red  granite pictures  which was run by najib's stepson with  the money from low  the studio made the wolf of wall street  this is the greatest company in the  world  it was never clear exactly what lowe did  at 1mdb and why he was even there  in investment banking you never want  someone hanging around the hoop who  doesn't  have a good reason to be there  especially when there's public entities  involved  because it's often a sign that someone's  getting a take  but those days are over in october low  agreed to forfeit more than 700  million dollars in assets u.s  authorities sought to seize  including real estate a luxury yacht and  a private jet  according to a settlement load did this  without pleading guilty  and has denied any wrongdoing blow is  also missing he's a kind of  one of the world's biggest global  financial fugitives  and based somewhere in china though we  don't know entirely where  as the scandal unfolded najib was able  to squash some of the investigations  internally  but in 2018 he lost his bid for  re-election  his opponent ran on an anti-corruption  platform  matt then unraveled everything for najib  they raided his house  they found boxes of cash they found  millions of dollars in jewels  last month the malaysian court sentenced  him to 12 years imprisonment and fined  him nearly 50 million dollars  in what will be the first in a string of  cases against the former prime minister  najib has denied wrongdoing and his  lawyer said najib would appeal the  court's decision  as for lysner he is no longer with  goldman he pled guilty in 2018 to  conspiring to launder money and violate  foreign anti-bribery laws  he'll likely be sentenced but in the  meantime he's cooperating with the us  government as a witness  against other parties including his  former employer  for goldman this scandal may have just  come to a close with the bank agreeing  to pay about 2.8 billion dollars to the  us government and admit wrongdoing  according to people familiar with the  matter this settlement follows one  earlier this month with the government  of malaysia  where the bank agreed to pay two and a  half billion dollars  it's not an accident that the investment  bank at the center of this  is goldman sachs it's a firm that prides  itself on  being a little bit edgier and it has  worked out remarkably well for them  for a long time but every 10 or 15 years  it blows up and it always blows up in  sort of an unpredictable  way even with goldman's settlement the  1mdb saga continues  much of what mdb's missing billions is  still unaccounted for  and the only one i think who really  knows where everything  is is jolo and he has no interest in  telling anyone at this point so  a lot of that may stay secret i think  it's going to take a long time and we  may never know the full extent  of what happened in 1mdb
 

